# Utah Birds: When Do Utah's Birds Show Up?

A custom dataset of research-grade bird observations in Utah during 2025, built by combining the
[iNaturalist API](https://api.inaturalist.org/v1/docs/) with species traits from
[AVONET](https://doi.org/10.1111/ele.13898). It was made for the STAT 386 Data Acquisition project.

**Question of interest:** How does the mix of bird species observed in Utah change across the year,
and do migratory birds differ from year-round residents in when and where they are reported?

The blog post that walks through this project is on my site: [link to blog post].

## Repository contents

| File | What it is |
|------|------------|
| `collect_data.py` | Downloads observations from iNaturalist, merges AVONET traits, and writes the CSVs |
| `data/utah_birds.csv` | Final dataset (CC0 / CC BY observations only) |
| `data/unmatched_species.csv` | Species that had no AVONET match, for hand-checking |
| `eda.qmd` | Exploratory data analysis |

Not committed: `data/raw/` (cached API responses), `data/utah_birds_full.csv` (includes records
with non-commercial or all-rights-reserved licenses), and the AVONET Excel file.

## Reproducing the dataset

1. Clone the repo and install the packages:
   ```bash
   uv sync          # or: uv add requests pandas openpyxl matplotlib
   ```
2. Download **AVONET Supplementary dataset 1.xlsx** from the
   [AVONET figshare page](https://figshare.com/s/b990722d72a26b5bfead) and save it to `data/`.
3. Put your own contact email in the `User-Agent` line of `collect_data.py`.
4. Run:
   ```bash
   uv run python collect_data.py
   ```
   A full year takes about 2–3 minutes because the script pauses one second between requests.
   Re-runs read from the cache and finish almost instantly.

No API key is needed. iNaturalist's read-only endpoints are public.

## Data dictionary (`data/utah_birds.csv`)

| Column | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `obs_id` | integer | iNaturalist observation ID |
| `observed_on` | date | Date the bird was observed |
| `month`, `day_of_year` | integer | Derived from `observed_on` |
| `season` | categorical | Winter (Dec–Feb), spring, summer, or fall |
| `latitude`, `longitude` | numeric | Location (obscured for some species and users) |
| `positional_accuracy_m` | numeric | Location uncertainty in meters (often missing) |
| `coords_obscured` | boolean | Whether iNaturalist obscured the coordinates |
| `common_name`, `scientific_name` | categorical | Species names (subspecies collapsed to species) |
| `id_agreements` | integer | Number of community identifications agreeing with the taxon |
| `license` | categorical | Observation license (`cc0` or `cc-by` in this file) |
| `family`, `order` | categorical | Taxonomic family and order (AVONET) |
| `body_mass_g` | numeric | Average species body mass in grams (AVONET) |
| `migration` | categorical | Sedentary, partial migrant, or migratory (AVONET) |
| `habitat`, `trophic_level` | categorical | Primary habitat and diet level (AVONET) |

## Responsible collection

- Requests are paced at one per second, well under iNaturalist's requested 60 per minute, and every
  response is cached so nothing is downloaded twice.
- The script follows iNaturalist's
  [API Recommended Practices](https://www.inaturalist.org/pages/api+recommended+practices) and
  identifies itself with a User-Agent.
- No usernames, user IDs, photos, or free-text location descriptions are kept.
- Coordinates that iNaturalist obscured (for threatened species or by the observer's choice) are left obscured.
- Only CC0 and CC BY observations are published here.

## Sources and citation

- iNaturalist contributors. iNaturalist observations, accessed via the iNaturalist API v1.
- Tobias, J. A., et al. (2022). AVONET: morphological, ecological and geographical data for all birds.
  *Ecology Letters*, 25(3), 581–597. Licensed CC BY 4.0.
